## Declared unit boundary

The exact whole Original is `CalcApproximateViewFactors`, `HeatBalanceIntRadExchange.cc:1406–1519`, with declaration 109–116. Native admission requires finite supplied area/azimuth/tilt, actual unique one-based registry positions, a complete ordered SPtr permutation, and Wall/Floor/Roof/Ceiling classes. Ceiling deliberately maps to Native Roof. IntMass, other excluded classes and nonfinite supplied values are outside this contract. Native empty arrays and Rust-only association/representation errors are unpaired.

The 21 frozen input-only records cover the required source decisions:

| Required behavior | Frozen cases |
|---|---|
| Equal and asymmetric areas; directed F(j,i) axes | `positive-below-epsilon`; `asymmetric-areas` |
| Strict azimuth >10 and <350, no wrap normalization | `azimuth-at10`, `azimuth-above10`, `azimuth-at350`, `azimuth-below350`, `azimuth-360` |
| Strict tilt >10 | `tilt-at10`, `tilt-above10` |
| Self and floor-to-floor exclusion; floor-to-roof visibility | `floor-floor-roof`, plus every matrix diagonal |
| Positive division below epsilon | `positive-below-epsilon` |
| Zero/negative seen area and ordered warning/continue association | `nonpositive-diagnostic`, excluded-angle cases, `one-direct-surface-diagnostic` |
| Caller pointer order and accumulation order | `accumulation-registry-order`, `accumulation-pointer-permutation` |
| Selected Ceiling class mapping | `declared-ceiling-maps-Native-roof` |
| Six declared CON membership/name templates | `CON-template-*`, explicitly supplied geometry rather than parsed production geometry |

There are 15 direct diagnostic/boundary records and six templates. The ordinary equal-area obligation is represented by the two equal positive areas in the tiny-positive case; it need not become a new required case merely because its magnitude is small. The frozen profile already compares every ZoneArea/F scalar, shape, value class and signed zero, plus copied inputs/IDs/order and typed warning identity/order. This is completion of the declared case obligations, not exhaustive proof over every finite f64 value, matrix size, or excluded Native input.

The helper calls the unchanged whole Original once per declared case with real allocated state and arrays. It observes ZoneArea before deallocation and all F entries, returns/partial observations and genuine diagnostics. The Rust public API retains ordered IDs, ZoneArea, F and typed warnings through the same shared kernel used by the legacy interface. No additional mathematical subhelper, history update or timestep transition is hidden in this direct routine.

The three Rust-only API checks (zone mismatch, duplicate ID, empty input) remain contract tests. They cannot count as paired Native failure cases. Global diagnostic backend delivery/index equality is separately unpaired; the required typed warning/continue identity and order are part of the direct comparison. No new unit test, tolerance change or input replacement is needed to repair a known omission in the admitted direct unit scope.

