Native radiant initialization selects representative surfaces, accumulates nonrepresentative areas and preserves reporting order at 496–574. For the ordinary no-user/no-shelf route with existing solar F, it copies the already corrected solar matrix at 610–614. Otherwise raw CalcApprox630 and Fix645 run on the same radiant owner, followed by CalcScriptF660. A correct trace must retain which route actually occurred; it must not require a second raw helper call on the ordinary solar-reuse route.

GEO-02 certifies the selected geometry producers and their geometric outputs. Its contract does not establish these enclosure memberships, SurfacePtr ordering, representative grouping, aggregate areas, solar/radiant reuse or the raw-to-corrected matrix handoff. The six RAD unit templates deliberately supply geometry independently of GetSurfaceData, so they do not close that producer connection.

Current Rust ordinary initialization produces geometry at `initialization.rs:104–116`, and `HeatBalanceSurfaceIndexes` groups actual surface positions by zone at `state.rs:139–203`. It has no retained solar/radiant enclosure raw/corrected owner. The new identity-bearing public RAD API is called by its unit example/tests only. The ordinary compatibility algorithm selects the ScriptF flat-access path; the surface iteration calls the legacy probe, rebuilding approximate/corrected/ScriptF matrices and dropping raw ZoneArea/warning ownership. Reuse of the correct shared arithmetic does not establish initialized caller timing or downstream ownership.

